ation · 4246 posts · 2021"},{"title":"Have You Ever Beta Orbited a Girl","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/have-you-ever-beta-orbited-a-girl/248693","site":"T Nation · 3018 posts · 2018"}],"news":[],"social":[],"web":[{"title":"Sodium bicarbonate - Wikipedia","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_bicarbonate"}]},"angle":{"goal":"Skin & grooming","chain":["Mild abrasive or alkaline rinse","Used on teeth, skin or in the mouth","Proponents report cleaner-feeling skin and teeth"],"effect":"claimed","text":"People use baking soda and salt water as inexpensive cleansers and scrubs for skin and teeth, and baking soda as a pre-training supplement aimed at muscular endurance."},"wikipedia":null,"grokipedia":null,"lead":["Salt-water and sodium bicarbonate (baking soda) practices are household approaches that people fold into grooming routines: baking soda as a mild abrasive for teeth and skin, saltwater rinses, and baking soda as a sports supplement before hard training.[1] Proponents use them to support a cleaner-looking mouth and skin, and, through exercise capacity, a better physique.","Sodium bicarbonate is a common household compound used as an antacid, a mild abrasive, a deodorant ingredient and a sports supplement.[1] Salt-based face cleansers have also been patented, including a mineral-salt face-washing mask.[2]"],"infobox":[["Type","Folk / household practice"],["Main agents","Sodium bicarbonate, table or sea salt"],["Common uses","Mouth rinse, scrub, deodorant, sports supplement"],["Cost","Low"]],"sections":[{"h":"Description","paras":["Sodium bicarbonate is used in mouthwashes as a mild abrasive and acid neutraliser, in deodorants, and as an antacid.[1] A dissolved teaspoon in cooled boiled water has been described for cleaning the lash base in blepharitis, and a paste for insect bites.[1] It is also taken as a sports supplement to improve muscular endurance, with studies, mostly in males, suggesting it helps most in brief, intense efforts.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Reported risks","paras":["Sodium bicarbonate is classed as causing serious eye irritation, and excess intake can cause alkalosis.[1] The American Cancer Society has warned against using it as a cancer treatment, citing unproven effectiveness and potential harm.[1]"],"subs":[]},{"h":"Clinical studies","paras":["No studies found for salt-water or baking-soda facial routines as such. Related research on sodium bicarbonate as an exercise supplement is described in the general sodium bicarbonate literature.[1]"],"subs":[]}],"lore":{"intro":"Community discussions mention salt and bicarbonate mostly in passing, in training logs and diet threads, with salt intake often raised in sports contexts.[3]","claims":[{"claim":"Baking soda works as a cheap face or teeth scrub.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Baking soda before training improves endurance.","verdict":"unknown","note":""},{"claim":"Baking soda treats serious disease such as cancer.","verdict":"unknown","note":""}]},"timeline":[],"refs":[{"title":"Sodium bicarbonate","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_bicarbonate","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"type":"encyclopedia"},{"title":"Mineral salt face cleaning pack (patent CN101011329)","url":"https://europepmc.org/article/PAT/CN101011329","source":"Europe PMC","year":2007,"type":"study"},{"title":"T Nation forum \"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)\"","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/264067","source":"T Nation","year":2020,"type":"forum"}],"studies":[{"title":"Sodium bicarbonate","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Sodium_bicarbonate","source":"Wikipedia","year":2025,"kind":null}],"reddit":[],"forums":[{"title":"Flame Free Confession III: Even More Flame Free (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/flame-free-confession-iii-even-more-flame-free-part-1/264067","site":"T Nation · 10000 posts · 2020"},{"title":"Simo - The Red Shoe Diaries (Part 1)","url":"https://t-nation.com/t/simo-t